   "turn": 7,
   "response_text": "Perfect! I found the issue. Looking at lines 182-183:\n\n```python\ninput_dim = X_train.shape[1]\ninput_dim = mcfg.get(\"input_dim\", input_dim)\n```\n\nThe code first determines the actual input dimension from the data shape, but then OVERRIDES it with the config value if present. The config has `input_dim: 1`, but the actual data has 105 features (as shown by the error message `256x105`).\n\nThe problem is that the config specifies `input_dim: 1` when it should be `input_dim: 105`. This is a configuration parameter fault.\n\nLet me verify this is the actual root cause by checking the datautil to understand the data better:",
