  {
   "turn": 9,
   "response_text": "Perfect! Now I have the full picture. The training code:\n1. Loads X_train from a file which has 105 features (as shown by the error)\n2. Optionally adds an auxiliary feature (but this is not enabled in the config)\n3. Gets the actual input_dim from the data shape: `input_dim = X_train.shape[1]` (which would be 105)\n4. BUT then overrides it with the config value: `input_dim = mcfg.get(\"input_dim\", input_dim)` which uses the config's `input_dim: 1`\n5. Creates a model that expects 1 input feature\n6. When training starts, the model receives batches of shape (256, 105) and fails\n\nThe root cause is clear: **the config has `model.input_dim: 1` when it should be `105`**.\n\nLet me gather the evidence and prepare my submission:",
